  "discussion": {
    "headline": "fairly quiet week with up-and-down temperatures",
    "dateLine": "11:15 a.m. Tuesday, September 15, 2026",
    "excerpt": "In the wake of Sunday night's cold frontal passage, northerly winds of 10-20 mph ushered much cooler and drier air into the Lower Susquehanna Valley on Monday. Despite mostly sunny skies, high temperatures only reached the mid-to-upper 70s, and dewpoints fell into the upper 40s by the afternoon hours. In fact, this morning's low of 48°F at Millersville University was the first sub-50°F reading since June 2.. a span of over 100 days (see below). …",
